  "certified_type": {
    "category": "Load cell",
    "type_designations": ["KIS-11"],
    "module_designation": "Analog load cell",
    "description": "KIS-11 is an analog-passive shear beam load cell supported at one end with the load applied at the other end. KIS-11 has strain gauges that measure the strain arising from the shear forces caused by the load. KIS-11 has a sleeve, which makes it possible to apply the load directly over the strain gauges, eliminating disturbing effects from bending forces. The strain gauges are placed in an I-beam section and are oriented for optimal measurement of the shear force. The load cell is provided with a shielded cable; the shield is not connected to the load cell body. The cable has four wires plus shield, with the ground open at the load cell end. Wiring: RED/GREEN +Excitation, BLACK -Excitation, GREEN/WHITE +Signal, WHITE/RED -Signal. Markings contain the cell type, manufacturer name, serial number, and Emax."
